Independent cross-platform watcher risk QA finding; WIP, no native qualification.

Exact Windows source: `a69a1ea853d617048649f55e3c74661ad21a51a8` (PR #3952); `git diff 3cc6fdb22797dec39c4252deeb2240e288243329 a69a1ea853d617048649f55e3c74661ad21a51a8 -- src/article-vault/windows tests/article-vault/windows` is empty. Canonical implementation owner: `01a119f2-8d36-775e-92e4-17db390ff03c`, issue #2670.

Actual compiled `WindowsVaultRawFactCodec.Verify` accepts resealed contradictory raw facts. Expected: shape/privacy/closed-semantics refusal independently of the digest; actual: `true` for 10 negative controls:

- restart and overflow clear both `RescanRequired` and `ReasonCode`;
- native action 4 labeled `Modified`;
- rename-old carries only a new path or carries both old and new paths;
- a modified fact carries no path;
- failure reason contains a free-text/body/token-shaped string instead of a stable reason code;
- timestamps are zero/negative;
- `Source` disposition carries `..\outside.md`;
- independently expected identity and fact both claim `ext4` on the Windows schema.

The strongest confirmed defect is the missing raw event-shape and mandatory-failure semantic validation. The lexical Source-path and identity cases additionally expose declaration validation gaps; native reparse/root admission remains #2109-owned and is not exercised here. No running native observer or exploitation was attempted; production construction remains closed and resealed clean-watermark/body-digest promotion is correctly refused.

Reproduction in this isolated QA workspace:

```bash
source /workspace/.setup/activate.sh
dotnet build /workspace/watcher-parity-risk/WatcherParityRisk.csproj -c Release
dotnet /workspace/watcher-parity-risk/bin/Release/net10.0/WatcherParityRisk.dll
```

Build exit 0; executable exit 1; JSONL result 22 PASS / 10 FAIL. Evidence: `/workspace/watcher-parity-risk/evidence/parity.jsonl`, `/workspace/watcher-parity-risk/evidence/parity.exit`; harness source: `/workspace/watcher-parity-risk/Program.cs`. No production/shared project/registry/checker/baseline files edited.

Other exact inputs: macOS `0538404eba4c6818db5ff02f057ac2650d6d97d3`; snapshot/event source `7bab017f162852eea4f8c7888e1bccfcc9b3b9ea` (newer published PR #3977, includes canonical APIs). macOS counterpart refusal controls pass. Actual original Linux raw-fact adapter → canonical normalizer → interrupted rescan → structural completion remains blocking; resealed obligation deletion is refused. Windows queue loss marker and subsequent sequence gap remain observable; native decoder preserves duplicate/reverse rename ordering and reports a truncated tail after the auditable prefix.

Windows NTFS and macOS APFS native behavior are UNRUN here (Linux host); Darwin C is not compiled. These managed controls are not platform acceptance. Continuing independent declaration/native binding and composite checks; do not wait for a larger suite/archive to act on this finding.

Final exact source check: PR4000 head `cb7d81403a4893c84a065b18fb6675947af7b173`, branch codex/vault-dependency-candidates-2126-2129. Original Release project relevant regression 217 passed / 0 failed / 0 skipped at this head; actual FsUsUI alias grammar 25/25 + focused Vue TSC/local-source ESLint pass; commit-range/repository checks pass. Canonical four Dependency modules + schema compare byte-identical to 00eeaf705dcc03a5412b36002df0b166e7442f3a. Final matrix entry still fails same parser identity/authority closure d732 vs dae33; original lifecycle failure remains Linux backslash intermediate-path handling despite real Debug output. FsUsUI unchanged f2b3bb89ffe5f749da26c388f058efdbb6aee864; both worktrees clean. Earlier failure logs retained; no automatic pass.

